error: `getUnchecked` is for the language's own module only
  it reads an item without checking its index, which only `std` does, where the index is known to be inside
  --> error_get_unchecked_outside_std.sg:5:26
 5 |     print(unsafe numbers.getUnchecked(1))
   |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  hint: `numbers[i]`, which checks the index, or `numbers.get(i)`, which gives `null` past the end
